WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.250
If you want to know how Pennywise lived on
after the events of It, then stick around

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.880
to the end of this video.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.190
Hello and welcome to Horror History.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:16.500
My name is Professor CZsWorld, also known
as Shaggy, also known as Emo Abraham Lincoln

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.359
and in today’s lesson we’ll be discussing
one of Stephen King’s most iconic monsters:

00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:25.289
Pennywise, also known as It, also known as
The Deadlights also known as Robert Gray.

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:28.679
Stephen King hasn’t really gone on the record
about his inspirations for It, causing some

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.430
to believe that the events of the 1986 novel
actually happened.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:36.460
On the other hand, actual intelligent people
drew comparisons to a serial killer John

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:41.020
Wayne Gacy, a birthday clown in Chicago during
the 1970s who did unspeakable things to more

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.350
than thirty victims.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.800
He would later stash the kids in the crawlspace
of his basement, not so different than Pennywise’s

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.580
penchant for dragging his victims corpses
into the sewers below Derry, Maine.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.850
Pennywise in the movies is depicted as one
of the forms of a shapeshifting creature known

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:58.220
as It, who has resided in a lair at the bottom
Derry’s sewage system for hundreds of years.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:01.820
But in the novel, It is much more than that,
so let’s travel back to the inception of

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.380
It, over 1 billion years ago.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.780
[Horror History]

00:01:07.789 --> 00:01:11.740
In the beginning there was an endless void
known as the macroverse, which was inhabited

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.950
only by a celestial force referred to as “The
Other.”

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:19.189
The Other created two additional inhabitants
of the macroverse, one protector called Maturin

00:01:19.189 --> 00:01:22.170
The Turtle, and one shapeshifting entity called
The Deadlights.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.380
The two would become natural enemies.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.450
The Turtle was kind and all knowing, but did
not like to involve itself in any conflicts,

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:30.869
and so, stayed hidden in its shell most often.

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:34.420
At some point, The Turtle came out of its
shell with a stomach-ache and vomited out

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.420
our universe.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.069
Yeah, so everything you’re sitting in right
now?

00:01:37.069 --> 00:01:38.630
Yeah, that’s actually puke.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:39.630
Everything you’ve eaten today?

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:41.289
I think you get the idea.

00:01:41.289 --> 00:01:43.600
Speaking of which, It’s main form of sustenance
is fear.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:45.780
“I’ll take him.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.080
I’ll take all of you.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:53.999
And I’ll feast on your flesh as I feed on
your fear.”

00:01:53.999 --> 00:01:58.590
Because of that fact, It traveled to our universe
to look for food, much like how I may travel

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.109
to Taco Bell when I’m done filming this.

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:03.249
A couple thousand or possibly even million
years ago, It discovered Earth.

00:02:03.249 --> 00:02:07.829
Earth was basically like a buffet for It,
because humans have much more complex imaginations

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:09.970
than any species It had discovered before.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:13.850
Specifically, the imaginations of human children
were especially attractive to It, because

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.560
they were capable of an unprecedented level
of fear.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.920
It arrived on Earth as a fiery meteoric object
that crashed into the land in North America

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.730
that would one day become known as The Barrens
in Derry, Maine.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:28.680
The impact scared away the animal inhabitants,
such as antelope, fish, bats and others.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.350
The impact crater was devastating, but the
area would be taken back by trees and wildlife

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:33.350
over the years.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:37.100
The impact also sent It into a deep sleep,
possibly aided by the fact that it became

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.460
trapped in the ice age.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:42.950
In the year 1715, It would thaw out and arise
from this slumber, thus marking the beginning

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:47.290
of the cycle that would repeat roughly every
27 years, where It would awaken to feed on

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:51.280
the fear of Derry’s residents, not too different
than how some mammals may eat and then go

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.620
into hibernation during the winter.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.480
These incidents would often go unrecorded
in Derry’s history books, but that hasn’t

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.980
stopped locals from doing their own research.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.360
The earliest known victims of It, were a party
of 340 settlers called The Derry Company,

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.620
named after the town in Ireland from which
they hailed.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.140
They started to create a civilization along
the Kenduskeag River, and Derry Township became

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.210
a logging town.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.530
“Still is, am I right boys?”

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:17.700
In 1743, every single settler disappeared
without trace or explanation.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.200
"The entire camp?"

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:23.580
"There were rumors of Indians, but no sign of an attack."

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:27.840
The town was left deserted, other than one
single house that burned down on the same

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.140
spot where Georgie Denbrough would be killed
300 years later.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:34.910
I’m guessing all of these settlers were
eaten by It, because she had taken such a

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:38.910
long nap after crashing on Earth, and probably
woke up especially hungry.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:42.870
Shortly after Derry Township was rediscovered,
the town was re-established and the canal

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.540
was built for easy access to the Kenduskeag
river.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.850
It seems to be about this time that It starts
experimenting with using the form of a clown.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:54.840
A picture from Will Hanlon’s album dated
to the 1700s shows a funny looking man juggling

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.900
bowling pins on the street near the canal.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.180
He wasn’t wearing makeup, but did have the
recognizable tufts of hair.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:05.319
The next known event is in 1851, which is
four 27-year cycles after the disappearance

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:06.319
of the settlers.

00:04:06.319 --> 00:04:10.350
It targeted a man named John Markson, likely
using the power of the Deadlights to possess

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.780
him and do his bidding.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:15.850
It seems that humans who look directly into
the deadlights are put into a trancelike state

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.540
where they can be controlled by It.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:21.329
John poisoned his entire family, then killed
himself with a white nightshade mushroom.

00:04:21.329 --> 00:04:25.410
Keep in mind that having someone else do It’s
bidding doesn’t benefit It directly, but

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.400
what it does do is instill fear into everyone
involved, making them more delicious meals

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.400
for Pennywise.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.510
It’s basically the equivalent of putting
those little sauce packets on your taco.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:38.120
In 1856 -- the clown’s image appears in
a political cartoon amongst some drunken loggers

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.120
at a bar.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.220
This illustration seems to predict the next
cycle, which begins in 1877 -- when four separate

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:46.340
lynchings took place in town -- and carries
into 1879.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:50.160
Derry’s logging business was really booming
at that time, and a group of lumberjacks stumbled

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:53.820
across another group, finding them completely
hacked to pieces.

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:57.450
Like a bear coming out of hibernation, It
would continue to come out every 27 years

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:00.460
or so to cause mayhem and feed on the fear
of the residents of Derry.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.540
The next cycle was especially bloody.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:07.120
Coming up next, we’ll go into the horrifying
archives produced by It in the early 1900s.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:15.360
I had a ton of people participate in the last
giveaway, and since you were all so excited

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.370
about that one, I though, why not just do
another giveaway?

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:22.230
This time, you’ll float too, because the
winner will be taking home this Float.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.230
Merchandise.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:26.820
To enter, make sure you’re following CZsWorld
on Instagram and like this post.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:28.210
Winner will be chosen at random.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:31.620
Full rules can be found in the video description.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:40.160
In 1891, an ironworks is built in Derry by
the Kitchener family, and an article about

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.470
the opening of this facility is featured in
the paper.

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:46.120
The frontpage photograph shows a crowd gathering
to celebrate the cutting of the ribbon, and

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:50.250
off the left of the crowd, a clown can be
seen celebrating with a handspring.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.710
This would be a precursor to one of Derry’s
deadliest events that took place at the end

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:54.710
of this cycle.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:58.370
But first, there was a major incident that
took place shortly after It’s reawakening

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.580
in September of 1905.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:04.370
The logging business in Derry had become big
enough that people started to organize unions.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.560
One of these organizers was named Claude Heroux.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:09.990
He and three colleagues were staying in a
hotel in Derry, and during this stay, the

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:13.490
colleagues turned up dead in the Kenduskeag
River with missing body parts and the word

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.080
“union” pasted on each of their backs.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:19.650
It’s unclear if this was the result of Pennywise’s
actions or if it was legitimately just unhappy

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:23.930
workers, but Heroux, in an act of revenge,
took an axe to a bar called The Silver Dollar

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.310
and took out the loggers he thought were responsible.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:28.490
That night, the townspeople rioted.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.400
After Heroux’s arrest, they dragged him
out of his jail cell and lynched him on the

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:32.400
side of town.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.430
One witness mentioned there was a guy there
doing tricks and flips, who he assumed was

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:38.520
new in town, but noted that he seemed to stick
around after that.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:42.430
This highlights one of the major strengths
of Pennywise, other than fabulous gymnastics

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:45.740
skills, It has the ability to divide people
and turn them against each other.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:49.139
It would later attempt to use this tactic
on the Loser’s Club after Eddie Kaspbrak

00:06:49.139 --> 00:06:53.170
suffers a broken arm, but their strong unity
ends up working as an advantage to them.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:57.169
But before we get there, there’s a lot more
of Pennywise’s history in Derry to cover.

00:06:57.169 --> 00:07:00.770
In 1906, an unexplained slew of animal mutilations
takes place.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.580
These are most likely also connected to It.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:06.180
Now sometimes when you’ve just eaten tacos,
you’re a little hungry still, and you say,

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:10.270
“you know what, I’m gonna grab a big burrito,
maybe some nachos and a large soft drink for

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:11.270
the road.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:14.110
And that’s basically what Pennywise did
before going back into hibernation.

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:18.680
On Easter of 1906, the previously mentioned
Ironworks held an Easter egg hunt for all

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:24.070
the kids in Derry during which, the place
exploded, leaving 102 dead, 88 of which were

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:24.560
children.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:28.740
At this point, it’s very clear that, A:
there’s a problem plaguing Derry, and B:

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:32.710
it’s occurring on a 27-year cycle, although
only a select number of Derry historians are

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:36.470
aware of it because Pennywise has actively
used its power to ensure that these disasters

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:37.710
stay out of the news.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:40.960
The disasters that took place from there on
out were largely ignored by the older townspeople,

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:44.370
who were starting to become despondent, and
preferred to ignore the problems rather than

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:45.370
acknowledge them.

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:48.479
It starts to feel like Derry is just cursed
with random acts of violence, but there’s

00:07:48.479 --> 00:07:50.360
no doubt that It is behind them.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:55.160
In 1929, a huge group of citizens gun down
the notorious Bradley Gang, and several witnesses

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.660
were said to have seen a clown participate
in the brutal shooting.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.860
Probably looked like something out of The
Dark Knight, minus the school bus….

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:04.570
Each of the witnesses to the Bradley Gang
execution claimed the clown had the same gun

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:07.530
as their own, though none of them shared the
same gun.

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:10.979
In 1930, was the first confirmed sighting
of one of the other recurring forms of It.

00:08:10.979 --> 00:08:15.340
The giant bird that would later attack Michael
Hanlon was first spotted 28 years beforehand

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.210
by his father Will Hanlon.

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:20.840
This happened the night of the horrible attack
on The Black Spot nightclub, in which a racist

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:25.060
organisation called the legion of white decency
burned down the popular African American run

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:28.810
jazz joint and the place collapsed before
dozens of people had the chance to escape.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:32.460
Just after narrowly making it out, Will looked
up and saw a giant bird with red balloons

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:36.200
tied to its wings, a detail he kept to himself
until he was on his deathbed.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:40.380
From here on, Will knew that Derry was no
ordinary town, but he would never fully understand

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:43.430
that It was responsible like his son would
one day find out.

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:46.640
The following year, one of the worst floods
in town history occurred.

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.730
This flood was almost as bad as the flood
that occurred in my comment section that one

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:53.170
time when I had the wrinkly shirt, and this
flood uncoincidentally took place during one

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.460
of Pennywise’s waking years.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:58.440
Stephen King doesn’t specifically note when
the sewer system that runs under Derry was

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:01.730
built, but there’s a good chance, based
on when certain laws went into effect in real

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:04.700
life, that it was around the time of this
big flood in the book.

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:07.870
While these systems may have been implemented
to keep water levels from overflowing to prevent

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:11.800
another disastrous flood, they would inadvertently
become the home of Pennywise, who built his

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.890
lair deep within the sewers under Derry.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:17.170
From this point forward, future sightings
of Pennywise the Dancing Clown are all connected

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:21.320
to the drain system, whether it be a creepy
voice echoing from a drain, a glowing yellow

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:25.670
pair of eyes emanating in a sewer grate or
a mysterious red balloon floating around in

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:26.660
a run-off pipe.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.540
“There’s been another murder.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.400
Little Velma Daniels.”

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:32.640
“Velma Daniels?”

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:35.440
“Her poor body was found this morning down
by the canal.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:39.380
So if you come down here to play, come together
like you are now, understand?”

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:43.940
Another image in Will Hanlon’s photo-album
shows the celebration at Wally’s Spa in

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:46.320
1933 when the US alcohol prohibition ends.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:50.370
The group photo contains many men holding
up beer mugs, and Pennywise drinking champagne

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.020
from a high heeled shoe in the corner.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:55.130
Pennywise continues to make appearances throughout
Derry’s history.

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:59.850
For example, in 1945, when Japan surrendered
to end World War II, a parade is held in Derry

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:03.630
to celebrate, and in one photograph, the clown
can be seen dancing in the background.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:07.610
In the 50s, Pennywise would bring this same
photo to life to terrorize the Loser’s Club,

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:11.240
but that is just one of the many events that
took place after the tragic incident involving

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.560
Georgie Denbrough in 1957.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:16.910
Coming up, we’ll be analysing one of the
darkest cycles of It’s history in Derry,

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:20.480
and the reasons behind this particular spree
being cut short.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.740
It was a rainy October day in 1957.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:34.300
Naturally, as a 6-year old boy, Georgie Denbrough
wanted to go out and play in it.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:38.279
He suited up in his yellow rain jacket and
asked his big brother Bill to make him a paper

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:38.780
boat.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:39.640
"There you go."

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:43.460
The boat was pushed along the gutter in the
Derry Public Works drain system, which was

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:45.440
managed by his father, Zack Denbrough.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:50.141
The boat began to pick up speed, and not wanting
to lose it, little Georgie raced after, not

00:10:50.141 --> 00:10:53.560
knowing that he was rushing into his own watery
tomb.

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:56.880
He was unable to grab his boat before it was
washed into the sewer grate, where a man in

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:03.760
clown makeup introduced himself as Mr. Robert
Gray, otherwise known as Pennywise the Dancing

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.800
Clown.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:08.640
Pennywise did not immediately become aggressive,
first, befriending Georgie and tempting him

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.589
to reach into the grate and get his boat.

00:11:10.589 --> 00:11:15.529
This is the very reason that the shapeshifting
It so often opted to use the clown form: Pennywise,

00:11:15.529 --> 00:11:19.130
because most children love clowns… or at
least they did back then before THESE came

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:20.130
out…

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.890
Today he would probably take the form of some
Fortnite YouTuber or something.

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:26.570
But he would use the Pennywise form to lure
the children, because children have the most

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:30.140
active imaginations and so, make the richest
meals for It.

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:33.820
Once he has them drawn in, he brings out his
pulsing eyes and razor sharp teeth and devours

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:35.690
them while they are most afraid.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:37.950
Again, much like I do when I’m devouring
my tacos.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:41.990
That is the fate that meets young Georgie,
who is the first of a whole slew of deaths

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:44.170
and disappearances at the hand of It.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:47.240
Next was Betty Ripsom in December of 1957.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:50.830
Pennywise spoke to her through the drain in
her home to make her afraid before attacking

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.880
and leaving her body ripped apart near Outer
Jackson Street.

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:56.880
“Don’t tell me that’s…”

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.120
“Who’s sneaker is it?”

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:01.100
“It’s Betty Ripsom’s.”

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:04.870
Betty’s screams continued to echo through
the drains and haunt her parents for the rest

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:05.990
of this waking cycle.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:10.070
The next month, when school is back in session,
Ben Hanscom sees the clown standing on the

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:13.900
ice as he walks over the canal bridge and
Pennywise entices him to come down into the

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:17.370
sewers with the prospect of balloons, the
promise of never growing up, and making it

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:19.649
seem like the sewers are basically a fun fair.

00:12:19.649 --> 00:12:23.560
A hand reaches up onto the bridge, and Ben
recognizes it as the mummy from the horror

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.890
movie, The Mummy, but wearing a clown suit.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.810
Ben is able to escape, but the same cannot
be said for Cheryl Lamonica, who falls victim

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.010
to Pennywise that April.

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:34.370
Then, towards late April, a three year old
named Matthew Clements is abducted by Pennywise

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:38.040
while riding his tricycle around the house,
causing the police chief to put a curfew into

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:38.900
effect.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:42.140
Before the end of that Spring, Mike Hanlon
rides his bike to the remains of the Ironworks

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:46.440
that exploded in 1906, where he is attacked
by a giant bird, who rises out of the cellar

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:48.510
hole and swoops in to try to pick him up.

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:52.420
This is the same bird that his father saw
after the Black Spot fire, and combines Mike’s

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:55.660
fear of birds from when he attacked in his
crib as a baby, and the fear instilled the

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:57.800
night before by the movie Rodan.

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.950
*RODAN SCREECH*

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:03.150
Reminds me of the sound my 8th grade English
teacher used to use if you didn’t have proper

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:04.150
MLA format.

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:07.560
Mike is able to escape by cramming himself
into the remains of the smoke stack where

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.779
the bird couldn’t fit, and pelting it with
the tiles that were laying around.

00:13:10.779 --> 00:13:14.490
Mike feels some kind of force “helping”
him throw the tiles harder, which I believe

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:15.490
may have been the Turtle.

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:18.550
It was also around this time that Stan Uris
had his encounter with It.

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:22.310
He had been birdwatching in the park near
the Standpipe, a water reservoir that some

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:23.880
kids had drowned in the 1930s.

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:27.959
He hears a loud noise, and realizes that a
door at the base of the Standpipe had been

00:13:27.959 --> 00:13:28.959
blown open.

00:13:28.959 --> 00:13:33.000
He walks over to investigate when he hears
carnival music echoing through the dark.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.840
Squishy footsteps approach him.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:38.480
Stan calls out to ask who’s there, and gets
the response: “the dead ones.”

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:42.720
Before he escapes, he sees the figures of
the drowned kids with purple-ish black jeans

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.320
and orange pom-pom buttons.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:47.560
Stan’s friend Eddie Kaspbrak has a similar
experience with It.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:51.560
Eddie would sometimes play around the trainyard,
and one day a hobo with leprosy climbs out

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:55.490
from under the porch of an abandoned old house
-- number 29 Neibolt Street.

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:58.360
Eddie is a hypochondriac, so this has a major
effect on him.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:02.210
It uses this fact to her advantage when coming
up with a form to scare Eddie.

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:05.930
One day Eddie decides to check under the porch
to make sure nobody’s waiting for him there

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:10.660
and sees It in a form similar to the hobo,
but now crawling with disease and wearing

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:12.070
the silvery clown suit.

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:16.579
The Leper introduces itself as Bob Gray, and
crawls out from under the porch to chase Eddie

00:14:16.579 --> 00:14:17.579
away.

00:14:17.579 --> 00:14:21.680
Despite these four victims escaping, Pennywise
would continue to haunt them in their dreams.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:24.700
One night when Eddie is going to bed, he hears
the leper whisper, “it won’t do any good

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:25.850
to run”.

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:29.120
Then, at the beginning of the summer, Ben
has a dream where he’s playing baseball,

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:30.380
and he hits a home run.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:33.339
As he’s rounding the bases, he sees a clown
waving to him in the trees.

00:14:33.339 --> 00:14:37.209
He doesn’t remember the rest of the dream,
but wakes up with a wet pillow, as if he’d

00:14:37.209 --> 00:14:38.830
been weeping through the night.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.740
It is doing everything in its power to instill
fear in these members of the Loser’s Club

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:46.950
who escaped on the first attempt -- but what
would take place that summer would take things

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:50.100
to a level never before seen in Derry’s
history.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:00.800
Ever since the death of his younger brother
Georgie, Bill Denbrough has been having a

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:02.529
lot of disturbing thoughts.

00:15:02.529 --> 00:15:07.220
In June of 1958, Bill would go into Georgie’s
room to look at his photo album, and under

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:12.410
the influence of It, Georgie's school photo
winks at Bill and tells him, “see you soon.”

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:16.060
Bill drops the book and blood drips out of
the pages, but Bill’s parents would not

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.670
be able to see the blood like the kids of
Derry can.

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:21.240
This kicks off Pennywise’s busiest month
yet.

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:23.890
Another boy goes missing, this one named Edward
Corcoran.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:27.390
Edward was fleeing his abusive father and
decided to sleep in the park by the canal,

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:29.040
where someone grabs his ankle.

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.370
It takes on the form of Edward’s dead brother
Dorsey.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:34.600
When Edward ran, It took the form of The Creature
from the Black Lagoon.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:38.399
The last thing he sees is the creature’s
eyes going white, and a light leaking through

00:15:38.399 --> 00:15:42.550
the fins on It’s head -- this was most likely
Edward attempting to process the Deadlights.

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:45.700
Shortly after, Mike Hanlon finds Edward’s
knife near the spot he died.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:49.779
He hears a splash come from the canal, and
sees something move inside of a pipe.

00:15:49.779 --> 00:15:53.170
Mike runs away, but has the feeling that someone
is chasing him all the while.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:57.209
He would go on to share his experiences with
the rest of the Loser’s Club, who also explain

00:15:57.209 --> 00:15:58.360
their encounters.

00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:01.710
When Bill tells the story of his encounter
with Georgie’s photo book, Richie Tozier

00:16:01.710 --> 00:16:05.331
says he wants to see the album as well, so
Bill takes him over there, only to discover

00:16:05.331 --> 00:16:07.920
that Georgie’s school photo is missing from
the book.

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:12.860
Instead, there’s a photo of old Derry, somewhere
near the canal, and Bill and Richie see themselves

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.600
as a couple of sailors on the sidewalk.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:18.870
The picture begins to move, and Pennywise
pops up out of the canal, but he has the face

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:19.740
of Georgie.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:20.240
See?

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:23.440
These deepfakes are getting way too good --- oh
wait, wrong… century.

00:16:23.459 --> 00:16:27.490
At this point, the real Bill Denbrough reaches
into the photo, before Richie pulls his arm

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:29.889
back out to safety and closes the book.

00:16:29.889 --> 00:16:31.300
Bill’s hand is bleeding.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:34.370
This scene foreshadows the final confrontation
with Pennywise.

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:37.320
Bill and Richie have always been the ones
to directly confront Pennywise.

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:40.870
An important distinction is that they aren’t
the only ones to fight back, but they are

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:43.930
the two who are willing to take the fight
to It’s domain.

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:47.670
This incident also marks the first time that
Richie starts to realize that It is a monster

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:50.560
with supernatural properties rather than physical
ones.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.750
Bill and Richie would once again take the
fight to Pennywise’s domain when they decide

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:57.140
to go to 29 Neibolt Street to investigate
Eddie’s story about the Leper.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:17:00.829
They climb into the basement, and this time
It takes the form of the Teenage Werewolf

00:17:00.829 --> 00:17:04.130
that Richie saw when he and a few others went
to the movie theater.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:06.850
I feel like I would just start laughing if
my worst fear just kept turning into these

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:08.339
cheesy 50s horror movies.

00:17:08.339 --> 00:17:12.459
I can just imagine -- oh no, please don’t
kill me, and then the monster turns into…

00:17:12.459 --> 00:17:13.600
like, this guy.

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:17.199
I’d just be cracking up, but I’m sure
it was pretty scary at the time.

00:17:17.199 --> 00:17:21.429
Bill brings his father’s gun, but what ends
up hurting Pennywise more than the gun, is

00:17:21.429 --> 00:17:25.870
Richie screaming at it in his Irish Cop voice
and throwing sneezing powder back at it.

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:28.140
This is because It operates on belief.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:32.010
Just as their fear of it makes them juicier
targets, their confidence and childish humor

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.050
can be used to fight back against It.

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:37.730
By using the voice of an authority figure
and attacking the werewolf with something

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:41.880
that he believed would work, he’s fighting
It with the strongest weapon he has: his

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:42.680
imagination.

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.500
"Imaaagination!"

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:52.320
As they ride away on Bill’s bike, the clown
comes after them, wearing the same Derry High

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:54.790
School jacket that the werewolf had on moments
before.

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:58.610
It’s not really clear in the book if he’s
also wearing the clown suit, or if he’s

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:00.460
just naked under the jacket…

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:03.080
Actually I think I’ll just try not to think about
that.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:08.070
When they look back later, Pennywise has disappeared,
presumably taking refuge in a storm drain.

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:12.500
As we get into late June, Pennywise claims
a new victim, Veronica Grogan, a fourth grader

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.380
at the Neibolt Church Street School.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:17.910
Veronica would be one of the voices that Beverly
Marsh hears coming out of her drain later

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:21.890
that week, along with the other victims like
Matthew Clements and Betty Ripsom.

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:25.410
The drain spouts blood at her, but like the
blood from Georgie’s album, her father is

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:26.410
unable to see it.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:29.880
It tells Beverly that she’ll die if she
tries to fight, then the sink erupts with

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.230
blood once again.

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:35.630
The last incident of June occurs when Richie
Tozier is fleeing from some bullies, and dips

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:39.580
into the park at City Center, where there
is a statue of Paul Bunyan used to commemorate

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:41.120
Derry’s beginnings as a logging town.

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:45.580
The statue comes to to life and stares Richie
in the face, threatening to eat him.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:48.840
Moments after he runs for it, Paul Bunyan
destroys the bench that Richie had just been

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:50.250
sitting on with his giant axe.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:53.919
At the time, Richie chalks this up to being
some kind of bizarre dream, but he would later

00:18:53.919 --> 00:18:57.040
realize this was one of the many forms of
It.

00:18:57.040 --> 00:19:01.210
Not much happens in the first couple days
of July, outside of Eddie Kaspbrak momentarily

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:05.210
having a vision of a piranha wearing orange
pom-pom buttons while playing in the barrens.

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:09.169
The slow period is likely because It is preparing
to feast on a day when Derry’s children

00:19:09.169 --> 00:19:13.610
would be out in droves: July 4th, also known
as American Independence Day.

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:17.070
It’s kind of a shame It didn’t go with
Cinco de Mayo instead though, would have been

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:19.220
perfect for this taco analogy I’ve got going.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:22.530
July 4th would be the first time Mike saw
it in the form of Pennywise.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:26.350
He was playing in the marching band where
he saw the clown handing out balloons to kids

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.350
on the street.

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:30.960
The sight of Pennywise waving at him gave
him a similar feeling to the encounter with

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:31.960
the bird.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:35.520
Then, later on up the hill, he saw Pennywise
again, and wondered how he could have gotten

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.540
there so quickly.

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:40.390
This time, some of the kids he was handing
balloons to were crying, and again, Mike got

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:45.070
a bad feeling as he recognized the same clown
from all those old photos in his father’s

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:46.070
album.

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:49.400
It was most likely on this day that It claimed
the life of young Jimmy Cullum, and the rain

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:53.100
would push his body into the sunlight two
days later on July 6th.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:57.070
He was eventually found with peck wounds all
over his body, something that Mike would connect

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:58.650
to his encounter with the bird.

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:02.669
Jimmy would be the last random victim of It
that summer -- from this point on It would

00:20:02.669 --> 00:20:07.450
exclusively go after Bill Denbrough and his
gang of misfits or Henry Bowers and his gang

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:08.400
of bullies.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:19.950
One of the most notorious bullies in all of
Derry, perhaps even more feared than Henry

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:23.590
Bowers himself, was the 12-year old named
Patrick Hockstetter.

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:27.519
Even a sociopath like Patrick had fears of
his own for It to take advantage of though

00:20:27.519 --> 00:20:31.490
-- Patrick developed a fear of leeches while
visiting Brewster Lake when he was 7.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:34.880
During the summer when Patrick was 12, It
ambushed him at the junkyard, where he would

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:39.340
often go to deposit dogs and cats he had killed
around town in a discarded refrigerator.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:42.450
To his shock, these leeches were also able
to fly.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:46.530
Perhaps Patrick was so crazy that the leeches
were the only semblance of a true fear that

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:50.220
It was able to find in him, because as he
was being attacked, he saw a figure standing

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:51.220
there.

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:54.540
It was described as having a face running
like wax, as if he didn’t know what he wanted

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:55.540
to be.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:58.990
This is the only known instance that gives
any real insight about what it might look

00:20:58.990 --> 00:21:00.820
like while cycling among forms.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:04.970
Patrick would eventually pass out from blood
loss, only to wake up when it started devouring

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:05.970
him.

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:09.160
Beverly Marsh sees this incident with the
leeches as it’s happening, and after Patrick

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:13.880
is taken away, she hears Pennywise’s laughter
reverberating from a pumping station underground.

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:17.730
Four hours later, she brings all of her friends
to investigate, where they find a message

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:21.770
written inside the fridge in blood reading:
‘Stop now, before I kill you all, a word

00:21:21.770 --> 00:21:24.750
to the wise from your friend, Pennywise.”

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:28.620
Pennywise leaves The Losers a second warning,
because at this point each of them had survived

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:32.620
at least once, and the slightest hint of self
doubt begins to manifest itself within the

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:33.630
ancient creature.

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:36.990
This time, Mike borrows his father’s Derry
photo album -- the one that he recognized

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:40.510
the clown in the background of in all those
old photos . They stop at the photo of the

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:44.090
World War 2 parade, and like the photo that
appeared in Georgie’s photo album, this

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:48.330
one starts to move as well, only this time
instead of Bill reaching into the picture,

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:51.740
Pennywise rushes up towards them and hangs
on a lamppost in the foreground, threatening

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:56.280
once again to kill them all, his nose pressing
up on the plastic that the photo had been

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:57.280
encased in.

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:00.309
It rapidly changed forms to some of their
fears: Richie’s werewolf, Eddie’s leper,

00:22:00.309 --> 00:22:05.120
Ben’s mummy and Stan’s dead boys, at which
point Stan slams the album shut.

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:09.040
That’s when Bill starts to realize the truth:
It is afraid of them.

00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:12.809
What Bill hasn’t figured out quite yet is
that It is especially afraid of the power

00:22:12.809 --> 00:22:16.799
of their unity -- and that’s why It’s
next move comes against Eddie, while he’s

00:22:16.799 --> 00:22:17.990
alone and at his weakest.

00:22:17.990 --> 00:22:23.210
On July 20th, 1958, Henry Bowers and his friends
chase down Eddie and break his arm.

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:27.320
Eddie comes to during the ambulance ride and
briefly sees Pennywise behind the wheel.

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:31.490
That night, Eddie has a dream about his overprotective
mother telling off his friends who come to

00:22:31.490 --> 00:22:34.670
visit him at the hospital, by telling them
he doesn’t want to be friends with them

00:22:34.670 --> 00:22:38.832
anymore, which parallels a conversation that
happens at the same time in real life.

00:22:38.832 --> 00:22:42.770
In the dream, Pennywise is also in the hospital
waiting room - wildly dancing to celebrate

00:22:42.770 --> 00:22:44.380
the breaking up of the losers club.

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:48.370
The real life version of the conversation
is essentially the same, and It probably had

00:22:48.370 --> 00:22:52.140
some kind of influence over Mrs. Kaspbrak
to encourage her to try to remove Eddie’s

00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:56.210
friends from his life -- and this is further
suggested by the last image Eddie sees in

00:22:56.210 --> 00:23:00.960
the dream: It toggling among the many forms,
the last of which has his mother’s face.

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:04.611
The incident does cause some turmoil inside
the friend group, but that doesn’t stop

00:23:04.611 --> 00:23:07.570
them from reuniting to take on it once again.

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:11.200
On July 25th, the 7 Losers arrive at 29 Neibolt.

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:14.230
Each of them react differently to the house
based on their own fears.

00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:16.230
Upon entering, they find a white clown glove.

00:23:16.230 --> 00:23:20.330
They go upstairs, where they come across a
dirty magazine that winks at Ben.

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:24.620
The hallways they traverse shrink in on them
and eyes of the elves plastered on the wallpaper

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:25.800
begin to bleed.

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:29.740
It is doing everything It can to scare them
away without having to face them directly.

00:23:29.740 --> 00:23:31.360
They come across three doors.

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:34.820
The first contains a bed, which explodes and
oozes out black liquid.

00:23:34.820 --> 00:23:39.330
The second sounds like it has a loud buzzing
insect behind it, but turns out only to be

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:42.970
a mooseblower, which is essentially a can
that lets out a constant noise as sort of

00:23:42.970 --> 00:23:44.670
an audio scarecrow for farmers.

00:23:44.670 --> 00:23:48.929
The third door is just a bathroom, but the
toilet seems to have exploded, leaving white

00:23:48.929 --> 00:23:51.059
porcelain shards lying around the room.

00:23:51.059 --> 00:23:54.590
It quickly rushes up the pipe in what Ben
perceives to be It’s own form, which we

00:23:54.590 --> 00:23:55.770
know to be: the Deadlights.

00:23:55.770 --> 00:24:00.000
It explodes out of the pipe taking the form
of the werewolf and attacking Bill and Ben.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.960
Beverly fights back with the slingshot loaded
with silver ball bearings, which they believe

00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:06.669
to be effective based on the werewolf movies
they’ve seen.

00:24:06.669 --> 00:24:09.950
She hits the It on the snout with her last
shot, sending blood everywhere.

00:24:09.950 --> 00:24:12.110
However, the Losers are now defenseless.

00:24:12.110 --> 00:24:16.400
With no remaining ammo, Bev pulls back the
slingshot again and uses her belief to try

00:24:16.400 --> 00:24:20.660
to frighten It, sending It diving back into
the drain screaming, “I’ll kill you all!”

00:24:20.660 --> 00:24:21.660
“I’ll kill you all!”

00:24:21.660 --> 00:24:25.460
Not much happens in the next couple weeks
leading up to the big confrontation, but there

00:24:25.460 --> 00:24:30.070
is some activity from It, who is now more
afraid than ever of the Losers Club and their

00:24:30.070 --> 00:24:31.070
power.

00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:34.000
It decides decided to bring on a new ally,
one that won’t be limited by the power of

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:35.000
fear alone.

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:39.090
So It teams up with the next biggest enemy
of the Losers: Henry Bowers.

00:24:39.090 --> 00:24:42.520
After losing the switchblade that Henry had
attacked Ben with on the last day of school,

00:24:42.520 --> 00:24:43.890
Henry needed a new weapon.

00:24:43.890 --> 00:24:48.049
In early August, he saw some red balloons
tied to his mailbox with the faces of the

00:24:48.049 --> 00:24:49.049
Losers on each balloon.

00:24:49.049 --> 00:24:52.800
The balloons popped and the mailbox swung
down to show him the package.

00:24:52.800 --> 00:24:53.800
It was a knife.

00:24:53.800 --> 00:24:56.780
The return address simply said: Robert Grey.

00:24:56.780 --> 00:25:00.940
After this, Henry started hearing voices from
the moon, commanding him to kill his father,

00:25:00.940 --> 00:25:03.980
then telling him to get Victor and Belch to
help him go after Beverly Marsh.

00:25:03.980 --> 00:25:08.110
They end up chasing the Losers down into a
pumping station in the Barrens, which is connected

00:25:08.110 --> 00:25:09.840
to the sewer system where It lives.

00:25:09.840 --> 00:25:12.730
Victor and Belch reluctantly go down there
with Henry.

00:25:12.730 --> 00:25:16.880
I personally think that It senses their reluctance
and decides to take them out, first using

00:25:16.880 --> 00:25:21.190
the form of Frankenstein’s monster to decapitate
Victor, then tearing Belch’s face in half

00:25:21.190 --> 00:25:22.590
when he tries to fight back.

00:25:22.590 --> 00:25:26.400
Henry goes on after the losers, leaving Belch
to die at the hands of It.

00:25:26.400 --> 00:25:30.150
The Losers attempt to find It’s lair, letting
Eddie lead the way with his impeccable sense

00:25:30.150 --> 00:25:31.150
of direction.

00:25:31.150 --> 00:25:35.309
The are cut off, however, by It in the form
of a giant eye resembling the monster from

00:25:35.309 --> 00:25:37.180
a movie Richie had seen called The Crawling
Eye.

00:25:37.180 --> 00:25:39.400
Got to admit,  that one actually sounds kind of scary.

00:25:39.600 --> 00:25:43.659
Each of them is grabbed by one of the eye’s
six tentacles besides Eddie, who pretends

00:25:43.659 --> 00:25:48.400
his asthma aspirator is battery acid and sprays
the eye with it to help drive it away.

00:25:48.400 --> 00:25:52.420
Next, they’re attacked by the giant bird
form, but Stan uses his extensive knowledge

00:25:52.420 --> 00:25:56.491
of birds to determine that it isn’t a real
bird, and the fact that Stan doesn’t believe

00:25:56.491 --> 00:25:58.679
in It weakens the monster once more.

00:25:58.679 --> 00:26:03.200
The seven make it to a door containing the
lair of It -- a cathedral like chamber covered

00:26:03.200 --> 00:26:04.200
in spider webs.

00:26:04.200 --> 00:26:09.049
It is here that they encounter the true form
of it, an endless hairy crawling form composed

00:26:09.049 --> 00:26:13.440
of light, that their human minds can only
interpret as a giant spider, so that’s what

00:26:13.440 --> 00:26:17.180
they all see It as -- much to the dismay of
television audiences of the 90s.

00:26:17.360 --> 00:26:21.480
It goes after their leader, Bill, launching
him out of his physical body for a mental

00:26:21.480 --> 00:26:26.050
confrontation on what Stephen King describes
as the ballroom floor of eternity.

00:26:26.050 --> 00:26:29.860
The Turtle catches Bill, but tells him he
takes no stand in the conflict, that Bill

00:26:29.860 --> 00:26:31.010
must fight on his own.

00:26:31.010 --> 00:26:36.270
Bill then uses his mind to engage in something
known as The Ritual of Chud, then cries out

00:26:36.270 --> 00:26:39.799
the line, “he thrusts his fists against
the posts and still insists he sees the ghosts,”

00:26:39.799 --> 00:26:41.860
a phrase that was supposed to help him overcome
his stutter.

00:26:41.860 --> 00:26:42.860
“He thrusts his fists against the posts
and still insists he sees the ghosts.”

00:26:42.860 --> 00:26:47.179
Bill uses his faith in all the childish things
he believes in to mentally grab onto It’s

00:26:47.179 --> 00:26:49.580
mind and push himself back towards the real
world.

00:26:49.580 --> 00:26:53.780
It screams at Bill to let go as he rejoins
the circle of his friends in the real world.

00:26:53.780 --> 00:26:57.789
The Spider flees into the depths of her lair
-- and Eddie tells them all he could hear

00:26:57.789 --> 00:26:59.390
It, and that It was dying.

00:26:59.390 --> 00:27:03.450
All they could do is hope that they had defeated
the monster that haunted Derry and killed

00:27:03.450 --> 00:27:04.450
it.

00:27:04.450 --> 00:27:08.169
They make a blood pact to return to finish
job if It should ever rise again.

00:27:08.169 --> 00:27:14.090
So the 1957-1958 cycle ends prematurely, with
It going into an early sleep after the defeat

00:27:14.090 --> 00:27:15.640
at the hands of the Losers Club.

00:27:15.640 --> 00:27:21.299
But as always -- 27 years after the awakening
in 1957 -- It would come back with a vengeance

00:27:21.300 --> 00:27:25.700
on the people of Derry and those who had beaten
It so many years before.

00:27:34.840 --> 00:27:40.100
In July of 1984 a festival is held to celebrate
the anniversary of Derry’s canal.

00:27:40.100 --> 00:27:42.860
At the festival, there’s a little dispute
between two parties.

00:27:42.860 --> 00:27:46.919
On one side are the three guys Steve Dubay,
John Garton and Christopher Unwin.

00:27:46.919 --> 00:27:51.170
They were harassing a homosexual couple: Don
Haggerty and Adrian Mellon.

00:27:51.170 --> 00:27:55.210
The initial dispute is broken up by police,
but they have another confrontation later,

00:27:55.210 --> 00:28:00.350
where Garton and Dubay throw Mellon off of
a bridge where Pennywise the Clown waits below.

00:28:00.350 --> 00:28:04.640
Mellon might have survived the fall, but Pennywise
drags him under the bridge and bites into

00:28:04.640 --> 00:28:06.390
his armpit with huge teeth.

00:28:06.390 --> 00:28:10.690
At this time thousands of I ❤️ Derry balloons
similar to the balloon Mellon had earlier

00:28:10.690 --> 00:28:14.460
at the Derry Canal Days Festival emerge and
hit the bottom of the bridge.

00:28:14.460 --> 00:28:18.440
Mellon’s body is found with stab wounds,
bite marks and a missing armpit.

00:28:18.440 --> 00:28:22.059
Pennywise’s return parallels many of the
other tragedies occurring in Derry for the

00:28:22.059 --> 00:28:27.770
past 300+ years in one major way -- the incident
is largely ignored by witnesses and news outlets.

00:28:27.770 --> 00:28:32.289
However, this time there’s one person taking
special interest -- the town librarian, Michael

00:28:32.289 --> 00:28:36.700
Hanlon, one of the Losers who stayed in Derry
all these years to keep an eye out for It,

00:28:36.700 --> 00:28:38.440
should the creature ever return.

00:28:38.440 --> 00:28:41.690
Mike wanted to be sure that It was back before
contacting his old friends.

00:28:41.690 --> 00:28:46.830
He stood by as Pennywise claimed the life
of Lisa Albrecht on October 18th, then Steven

00:28:46.830 --> 00:28:49.179
Johnson at Memorial Park near the end of the
year.

00:28:49.179 --> 00:28:55.270
On February 14th 1985, two more children disappeared
-- Dennis Torio and Lori Anne Winterbarger.

00:28:55.270 --> 00:28:58.950
Dennis’s body was found in The Barrens with
a photo of Georgie Denbrough.

00:28:58.950 --> 00:29:03.040
This is the same photo that disappeared from
the photo album when Bill and Richie went

00:29:03.060 --> 00:29:04.710
to look in 1958.

00:29:04.710 --> 00:29:08.960
By March, Mike is pretty convinced that It
has come back, but wants to have proof before

00:29:08.960 --> 00:29:09.980
alerting the others.

00:29:09.980 --> 00:29:11.510
The bodies continue to pile up.

00:29:11.510 --> 00:29:15.770
Dawn Roy, a 13 year old girl, is found decapitated
in McCairn Park.

00:29:15.770 --> 00:29:20.840
On April 24th, 16-year-old Adam Terrault is
killed and mutilated by Pennywise.

00:29:20.840 --> 00:29:24.810
Two weeks later on May 6th, Pennywise emerges
through the pipes as 2 year old Frederick

00:29:24.810 --> 00:29:27.799
Cowan uses the restroom and drowns him in
the toilet bowl.

00:29:27.799 --> 00:29:32.370
His mother was outside and she heard screaming,
repeated flushing of the toilet and laughter

00:29:32.370 --> 00:29:34.070
that didn’t sound human.

00:29:34.070 --> 00:29:37.779
When she found her son, she had to be taken
to a mental hospital in Bangor.

00:29:37.779 --> 00:29:42.289
It was only one week after that when Jeffrey
Hollie was found torn open in Bassie Park

00:29:42.289 --> 00:29:43.440
near the canal.

00:29:43.440 --> 00:29:47.279
John Fury and Jerry Bellwood, two fifth grade
classmates, were killed before the end of

00:29:47.279 --> 00:29:48.279
May.

00:29:48.279 --> 00:29:51.460
Fury was found with his legs torn off under
the porch at 29 Neibolt Street and Bellwood

00:29:51.460 --> 00:29:55.580
turned up near a cement retaining wall on
Kansas Street with the words “come home”

00:29:55.580 --> 00:29:59.690
written over and over in blood -- a direct
message to Mike, who would soon make the six

00:29:59.690 --> 00:30:02.950
phone calls to remind his friends of the promise
they once made.

00:30:02.950 --> 00:30:06.070
The news was too much for Stan, who took his
own life.

00:30:06.070 --> 00:30:09.419
In the meantime, It would also be calling
back an old friend.

00:30:09.419 --> 00:30:13.340
Henry Bowers, who was sitting in Juniper Hill
Mental Asylum, began hearing the familiar

00:30:13.340 --> 00:30:15.980
voice of Pennywise speaking to him through
the moon.

00:30:15.980 --> 00:30:20.030
When the remaining Losers reconvened at a
Chinese restaurant upon returning to Derry,

00:30:20.030 --> 00:30:24.360
Pennywise leaves them warnings in their fortune
cookies including eyes, bugs, blood and more.

00:30:24.360 --> 00:30:28.330
This is a symbolic way for It to tell them
they’ll meet unhappy fortunes if they try

00:30:28.330 --> 00:30:29.330
to fight.

00:30:29.330 --> 00:30:32.720
The Losers go for individual walks around
town while they wait for their memories of

00:30:32.720 --> 00:30:34.620
the summer of ‘58 to come back.

00:30:34.620 --> 00:30:38.091
During this time, Pennywise terrorizes each
of them with the belief that they will not

00:30:38.091 --> 00:30:39.650
be able to win as they once did.

00:30:39.650 --> 00:30:43.330
I think the reason It becomes so confident
is a combination of factors.

00:30:43.330 --> 00:30:48.090
The Losers have grown up, lost their imaginations,
lost one of their members (Stan), and forgotten

00:30:48.090 --> 00:30:49.710
about Derry for the most part.

00:30:49.710 --> 00:30:53.850
However, one thing that I think It didn’t
count on was the fact that despite them growing

00:30:53.850 --> 00:30:56.370
older, many of them still work in creative
fields.

00:30:56.370 --> 00:31:00.990
Beverly designs dresses, Ben designs buildings,
Richie is a radio DJ known for his creative

00:31:00.990 --> 00:31:05.529
voices and Bill is an author of fiction -- a
concept that those people who think Pennywise

00:31:05.529 --> 00:31:07.640
is real don’t seem to understand.

00:31:07.640 --> 00:31:11.340
Each of the Losers goes somewhere they used
to spend time at in Derry.

00:31:11.340 --> 00:31:14.179
Ben visits the library where Pennywise taunts
him from the landing.

00:31:16.100 --> 00:31:20.180
“Excuse me sir -- do you have Prince Albert
in a can?

00:31:20.220 --> 00:31:21.560
You do?

00:31:21.560 --> 00:31:24.300
Well you better let the poor guy out -- HOO
HEH!

00:31:24.320 --> 00:31:24.880
HOO HEH!

00:31:24.880 --> 00:31:25.380
HOO HEH!”

00:31:25.400 --> 00:31:26.260
I love that part.

00:31:26.270 --> 00:31:30.590
It also scared Ben using the form of Dracula
and taunting him about the death of Stan.

00:31:30.590 --> 00:31:34.770
Before disappearing, it leaves behind a balloon
with a message, “have a good day, tonight

00:31:34.770 --> 00:31:35.770
you die.”

00:31:35.770 --> 00:31:38.581
In the movie -- Pennywise spends more time
warning the losers that they should get out

00:31:38.581 --> 00:31:42.179
of town, which really I don’t find to fall
in line with the character so much, because

00:31:42.179 --> 00:31:46.010
in the novel It comes back and wants revenge
on those who bested him -- so it wouldn’t

00:31:46.010 --> 00:31:49.929
really make sense for It to lure them all
back there and then make them leave again.

00:31:49.929 --> 00:31:54.020
Eddie takes his walk down memory lane… not
down memory lane because that probably isn’t

00:31:54.020 --> 00:31:58.240
a real place, but rather, down West Broadway,
where he comes upon the Tracker Bros truck

00:31:58.240 --> 00:32:00.270
depot or at least what’s left of it.

00:32:00.270 --> 00:32:02.030
This was were the kids used to play baseball.

00:32:02.030 --> 00:32:05.350
Eddie sees a leper version of Belch Huggins
climb over the fence.

00:32:05.350 --> 00:32:09.570
Then the canvas squares they used to use as
bases fly into the air and take after him.

00:32:09.570 --> 00:32:13.580
Tony Tracker, one of the co-owners of the
depot, comes out of the ground at home plate.

00:32:13.580 --> 00:32:18.530
Eddie also sees a zombie version of his childhood
crush Greta Bowie and of Patrick Hockstetter.

00:32:18.530 --> 00:32:21.940
Beverly goes back to her old apartment to
see if her Dad is still there, but a woman

00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:25.480
named Mrs. Kersh has taken up the residence
and invites her in for tea.

00:32:25.480 --> 00:32:29.270
Mrs. Kersh starts rotting before her eyes,
before dropping the fact that her father was

00:32:29.270 --> 00:32:32.380
Robert Gray, also known as Pennywise the Dancing
Clown.

00:32:32.380 --> 00:32:36.290
She also realizes that the tea she is drinking
tastes like crap from the sewer, and it is

00:32:36.290 --> 00:32:40.120
at this point that sis snapped... that meme’s
probably going to be so outdated by the time

00:32:40.120 --> 00:32:41.680
this video even comes out….

00:32:41.680 --> 00:32:45.850
Mrs. Kersh turns into a witch and chases Beverly
out as the whole place turns to candy like

00:32:45.850 --> 00:32:47.409
the house from Hansel and Gretel.

00:32:47.409 --> 00:32:51.240
As she runs out she hears her father's voice
call out, but when she turns back, she sees

00:32:51.240 --> 00:32:53.640
the clown holding the detached leg of a child.

00:32:53.640 --> 00:32:57.370
There’s also a balloon, with the words “It
Came From Outer Space” the name of a horror

00:32:57.370 --> 00:33:00.440
movie from the 50s that also works with the
origin of It.

00:33:00.440 --> 00:33:01.880
From It… by Stephen King.

00:33:01.880 --> 00:33:04.660
While I could probably go on about how many
times I’ve had an issue trying to distinguish

00:33:04.660 --> 00:33:08.320
the monster It from the word it, let’s instead
move on to Richie Tozier.

00:33:08.320 --> 00:33:12.230
Richie goes back to City Center, where the
Paul Bunyan statue turns into Pennywise holding

00:33:12.230 --> 00:33:15.850
two balloons, one reading “Richie Tozier’s
All-Dead Rock Show”.

00:33:15.850 --> 00:33:19.170
Pennywise tells him that the eye is waiting
for him below -- a reference to The Crawling

00:33:19.170 --> 00:33:21.630
Eye that they encountered on their first trip
into the sewers.

00:33:21.630 --> 00:33:25.850
He looks back up and the clown has been replaced
by a Buddy Holly statue and looking back on

00:33:25.850 --> 00:33:29.990
it now, it’s interesting to note that Pennywise
the Clown looked just like Buddy Holly roughly

00:33:29.990 --> 00:33:33.120
nine years before anyone knew who Rivers Cuomo
was.

00:33:33.120 --> 00:33:37.289
Richie feels a sharp pain in his eyes, possibly
a connection to the smoke in his eyes during

00:33:37.289 --> 00:33:39.270
the smoke hole ritual they did as kids.

00:33:39.270 --> 00:33:40.860
He blinks his contacts back to normal,

00:33:40.860 --> 00:33:44.020
and yes, this is me blinking for all you people who comment and say I never blink.

00:33:44.120 --> 00:33:46.240
and
everything goes back to normal, but he still

00:33:46.240 --> 00:33:48.640
hears Pennywise’s laughter in the back of
his head.

00:33:48.860 --> 00:33:53.100
Late that night, It takes the form of Victor
Criss to break Henry out of the mental asylum.

00:33:53.100 --> 00:33:57.070
Victor’s body still has the voice of Pennywise
though, and he explains that Henry must kill

00:33:57.070 --> 00:34:01.250
the Losers because Henry can hurt them regardless
of if they believe in him or fear him.

00:34:01.250 --> 00:34:05.309
In order to escape, they must first get past
one of the Juniper Hill guards, John Koontz.

00:34:05.309 --> 00:34:09.649
It first attacks him using the Pennywise form,
then turns into a giant dog -- which is a

00:34:09.649 --> 00:34:12.989
Doberman, just like the guard dogs at the
asylum -- and mauls Koontz to death.

00:34:12.989 --> 00:34:16.779
That night, the Losers reconvene at the library,
where It taunts them with strange visions

00:34:16.779 --> 00:34:21.019
including one of Stan’s 11 year old head
which is stuffed with feathers, possibly a

00:34:21.020 --> 00:34:23.560
reference to the often used bird form of it.

00:34:24.460 --> 00:34:25.720
"I finally made it guys.

00:34:25.900 --> 00:34:27.660
I'm in the Deadlights now.

00:34:27.660 --> 00:34:30.280
And you know what? It's true what they say.

00:34:30.500 --> 00:34:32.020
We all float down here.

00:34:32.320 --> 00:34:33.440
And you will too.

00:34:33.620 --> 00:34:36.960
in fact...THEY ALL FLOAT!

00:34:37.740 --> 00:34:40.320
His eyes open, and they are the eyes of Pennywise.

00:34:40.329 --> 00:34:42.790
The head bursts, leaving behind a mess of
blood.

00:34:42.790 --> 00:34:46.200
The Losers decide to call it a night, but
Henry Bowers has other ideas.

00:34:46.200 --> 00:34:49.179
Henry ambushes and attacks Mike, who is wrapping
up at the library.

00:34:49.179 --> 00:34:52.829
Then, while prowling the streets at 2AM, he
sees a sewer grate with a balloon tied to

00:34:52.829 --> 00:34:53.829
it.

00:34:53.829 --> 00:34:56.990
Don't waste your time on Henry because the
voice inside his head tells him that a ride

00:34:56.990 --> 00:35:00.319
has been sent for him and a 1958 Plymouth
Fury pulls up.

00:35:00.319 --> 00:35:04.200
I know this isn't an episode of Things You
Missed, this is Horror History, but let me

00:35:04.200 --> 00:35:08.259
give you a freebie anyways: the car matches
the description of Christine from another

00:35:08.259 --> 00:35:09.670
Stephen Book…

00:35:09.670 --> 00:35:10.670
Christine!

00:35:10.670 --> 00:35:14.339
The driver of the car was a zombie version
of Belch who doesn't speak the entire car

00:35:14.339 --> 00:35:18.299
ride until the end when Pennywise's voice
comes out of his mouth and tells him to shut

00:35:18.299 --> 00:35:19.569
up and get the losers.

00:35:19.569 --> 00:35:23.339
I can only imagine what kind of review Henry
would have left on zombie Uber.

00:35:23.339 --> 00:35:27.359
Henry would go on into the hotel and manage
to injure Eddie Kaspbrak, just as he did in

00:35:27.359 --> 00:35:33.039
1958, but in 1985, It had one more trick up
her sleeve that NONE of the Losers Club could

00:35:33.040 --> 00:35:35.600
have seen coming before the final showdown.

00:35:41.660 --> 00:35:44.420
Beverly Marsh never really escaped her abusive
father.

00:35:44.420 --> 00:35:49.380
Yes, she did get out of Derry, and yes, that
was the last time she ever spoke to her dad.

00:35:49.380 --> 00:35:53.170
But Beverly ended up falling into the same
old trap again when she married a man named

00:35:53.170 --> 00:35:56.459
Tom Rogan, who treated her even worse than
Al Marsh did.

00:35:56.459 --> 00:36:00.380
Tom was able ascertain Beverly’s location
after she left him to reunite with her childhood

00:36:00.380 --> 00:36:04.209
friends in Derry, and he found himself waking
up in a Holiday Inn in Maine where he found

00:36:04.209 --> 00:36:06.430
a balloon tied to his bathroom doorknob.

00:36:06.430 --> 00:36:10.229
The voice of It spoke to him through the balloon
and told him to do It’s bidding.

00:36:10.229 --> 00:36:13.039
At this point, I think it’s important to
look back at It’s human servants.

00:36:13.039 --> 00:36:17.250
The fact that It is able to manipulate some
people to do her bidding, but not others,

00:36:17.250 --> 00:36:18.410
is interesting to me.

00:36:18.410 --> 00:36:22.490
In fact, it seems that It is only able to
manipulate people who already have a lot of

00:36:22.490 --> 00:36:23.490
evil in them.

00:36:23.490 --> 00:36:27.010
There is also a nurse that It manipulates
later named Mark Lamonica -- the brother of

00:36:27.010 --> 00:36:29.500
Sheryl Lamonica who was killed in 1958.

00:36:29.500 --> 00:36:33.299
It sends him with a scalpel to try to finish
off Mike in the hospital -- and King describes

00:36:33.299 --> 00:36:36.450
him as being an easy target for It because
he’s a drug addict.

00:36:36.450 --> 00:36:40.450
On the other hand, it seems like It’s rival,
the Turtle is able to manipulate good people.

00:36:40.450 --> 00:36:44.140
The Losers Club members often describe some
kind of helping hand aiding them, like when

00:36:44.140 --> 00:36:47.520
Mike throws the tiles at the bird and he feels
something “helping” him throw them harder

00:36:47.520 --> 00:36:48.520
than usual.

00:36:48.520 --> 00:36:52.509
Now if only we could get the Cubs bullpen could get a little
help from The Turtle then we’d really be

00:36:52.509 --> 00:36:53.509
in business…

00:36:53.509 --> 00:36:56.369
But Beverly’s husband Tom isn’t the only
spouse who followed their partner into Derry,

00:36:56.369 --> 00:36:58.829
because Bill’s wife Audra has also made
the trip.

00:36:58.829 --> 00:37:03.229
In order to ensure the opportunity for revenge,
It uses Tom to capture Audra and bring her

00:37:03.229 --> 00:37:07.509
into the sewers, leaving her purse at the
foot of the pumping station as bait for Bill.

00:37:07.509 --> 00:37:12.479
Because of this, he, Eddie, Ben, Beverly and
Richie must go face It before they are ready,

00:37:12.479 --> 00:37:14.630
and this time, they’re on a rescue mission.

00:37:14.630 --> 00:37:19.190
Even with everything turned in It’s favor;
even with only 5 Losers to kill now as opposed

00:37:19.190 --> 00:37:23.890
to 7, It feels fear again as they approach,
so Pennywise tries to intimidate them a little

00:37:23.890 --> 00:37:25.950
more on their drive to the Barrens.

00:37:25.950 --> 00:37:29.549
Pennywise speaks through the car radio, first
reading an ad for the Richie Tozier All Dead

00:37:29.549 --> 00:37:30.549
Rock Show.

00:37:30.549 --> 00:37:33.670
Then Georgie’s voice berates Bill, telling
him “You let it kill me!”

00:37:33.670 --> 00:37:37.249
They turn off the radio, which must have been
a good indicator for It that Bill was still

00:37:37.249 --> 00:37:40.910
pretty rattled by the idea that he could have
been partially responsible for what happened

00:37:40.910 --> 00:37:41.910
to Georgie.

00:37:41.910 --> 00:37:44.880
I think it’s for this reason that the first
form that the adult Losers encounter after

00:37:44.880 --> 00:37:47.450
climbing down into the sewers is Bill’s
younger brother.

00:37:47.450 --> 00:37:50.730
Bill starts to feel guilt -- and he feels
he should have been the one to die.

00:37:50.730 --> 00:37:54.309
The others need him to come to the realization
that this Georgie isn’t real -- and he’s

00:37:54.309 --> 00:37:58.089
able to do so by repeating the phrase, “he
thrusts his fist against the posts and still

00:37:58.089 --> 00:37:59.609
insists he sees the ghosts.”

00:37:59.609 --> 00:38:02.829
Just like last time, this hurts It, who retreats
into the inner sanctum.

00:38:02.829 --> 00:38:07.229
You may have noticed throughout this video
that I refer to It using the female pronouns.

00:38:07.229 --> 00:38:10.930
There’s a reason for that -- and when they
get to the inner lair at the heart of the

00:38:10.930 --> 00:38:15.440
sewer system, they discover that the Deadlights
they interpret as a spider has an eggsack.

00:38:15.440 --> 00:38:17.109
It’s female and It’s pregnant.

00:38:17.109 --> 00:38:21.660
Thought I do have serious questions about
who, in their right mind, would have knocked

00:38:21.660 --> 00:38:22.300
It up.

00:38:22.500 --> 00:38:23.000
but...

00:38:23.240 --> 00:38:25.640
Actually let’s try not to think about that.

00:38:25.640 --> 00:38:29.230
Once again, It goes for Bill, which if you
think about it makes sense; he’s the leader,

00:38:29.230 --> 00:38:32.400
he’s probably the biggest threat to It seeing
as how he became a writer and he’s still

00:38:32.400 --> 00:38:35.800
flowing with creativity and It’s his wife
that’s been captured, so he’s

00:38:35.809 --> 00:38:36.800
the most motivated.

00:38:36.809 --> 00:38:40.150
Just like when they were young, Bill leaves
his physical body and enters the void.

00:38:40.150 --> 00:38:43.440
It tells him that The Turtle is dead, and
won’t be able to help him this time, which

00:38:43.440 --> 00:38:47.170
he doesn’t believe at first, but later concludes
to be true when they pass by The Turtle’s

00:38:47.170 --> 00:38:48.170
empty shell.

00:38:48.170 --> 00:38:51.459
Bill tried to mentally seize It’s tongue
like he had during the Ritual of Chud when

00:38:51.459 --> 00:38:55.539
they were kids, but this time he misses his
grip and drifts deeper into the void.

00:38:55.539 --> 00:38:59.579
In the physical chamber Richie realizes something
is wrong and confronts the spider using his

00:38:59.579 --> 00:39:00.579
Irish Cop voice.

00:39:00.579 --> 00:39:04.469
Then Richie is whacked into the cosmic void
as well, and he is able successfully engage

00:39:04.469 --> 00:39:05.819
in the Ritual of Chud.

00:39:05.819 --> 00:39:09.430
Richie takes Bill’s hand and threatens to
kill It if It doesn’t bring them back to

00:39:09.430 --> 00:39:10.430
the real world.

00:39:10.430 --> 00:39:13.920
They almost lose their grip on It, but are
able to safely get back to their physical

00:39:13.920 --> 00:39:14.920
bodies.

00:39:14.920 --> 00:39:17.940
Just before they arrive, Eddie is trying to
hurt The Spider with his aspirator like he

00:39:17.940 --> 00:39:22.480
did in 1958, but when It comes back to the
physical body of the spider, It bites down

00:39:22.480 --> 00:39:26.299
and rips Eddie’s arm off before retreating
into the dark depths of the lair.

00:39:26.299 --> 00:39:29.099
This time, Richie and Bill don’t want to
let It get away again.

00:39:29.099 --> 00:39:33.309
Just as they pursued It to 29 Neibolt Street
as kids, they follow the spider further into

00:39:33.309 --> 00:39:34.309
the dark.

00:39:34.309 --> 00:39:37.650
Beverly stops to comfort Eddie in his final
moments, while Ben finds the trail of eggs

00:39:37.650 --> 00:39:41.200
left behind by It, and one by one attempts
to stomp them all out.

00:39:41.200 --> 00:39:43.210
Now It was becoming more afraid than ever.

00:39:43.210 --> 00:39:44.969
It sensed Richie and Bill’s pursuit.

00:39:44.969 --> 00:39:46.709
It sensed the death of It’s young.

00:39:46.709 --> 00:39:48.140
And It began to turn white.

00:39:48.140 --> 00:39:52.150
It turned back to Richie and Bill, now beginning
to let off the Deadlights within.

00:39:52.150 --> 00:39:57.249
The arachnid creature begged them to let her
go offering them power, success and the prospect

00:39:57.249 --> 00:39:58.930
of 500 year lives.

00:39:58.930 --> 00:40:01.349
Bill and Richie began to feel the power of
“another”.

00:40:01.349 --> 00:40:06.150
Not It, not the Turtle, but the celestial
force I mentioned wayyyyyy back at the beginning

00:40:06.150 --> 00:40:10.140
of this video (even before I started talking
about tacos) that created both of them.

00:40:10.140 --> 00:40:13.380
Bill hears the sound of The Spider’s heart
pounding now like an enormous drum.

00:40:13.380 --> 00:40:17.529
He punches his way into It, reaches for the
heart and crushes it in his hand.

00:40:17.529 --> 00:40:21.119
The creature jerked and quivered, and as it
died, the light faded from it.

00:40:21.119 --> 00:40:24.859
Bill heard the voice of The Other telling
him, “son, you did real good.”

00:40:24.859 --> 00:40:27.200
Richie was basically passed out at this point.

00:40:27.200 --> 00:40:30.680
Ben had finished stomping over 100 eggs, and
thinks he’s gotten them all.

00:40:30.680 --> 00:40:34.400
Audra falls from the webbing she’s strung
up in and lies crumpled on the ground in a

00:40:34.400 --> 00:40:35.630
catatonic state.

00:40:35.630 --> 00:40:39.609
Eddie has died, and Beverly’s pack of matches
is their only source of light and hope to

00:40:39.609 --> 00:40:40.609
get out.

00:40:40.609 --> 00:40:44.910
Meanwhile, a huge storm brews above them over
Derry, and the flood that would ensue is a

00:40:44.910 --> 00:40:49.930
metaphorical washing out of all the bad history
the town had endured over the 300 or so years

00:40:49.930 --> 00:40:51.130
of its existence.

00:40:51.130 --> 00:40:55.099
The flood would end up destroying much of
Main Street and any buildings near the canal

00:40:55.099 --> 00:40:56.130
were swept away.

00:40:56.130 --> 00:40:59.640
The Losers were able to climb directly out
of the destroyed sewer pipes to the street

00:40:59.640 --> 00:41:00.640
above.

00:41:00.640 --> 00:41:04.859
As they left Derry, their memories of everything
that had happened between them and It began

00:41:04.859 --> 00:41:08.869
to fade once again, but this time, even Mike,
who was still recovering in the hospital,

00:41:08.869 --> 00:41:14.019
would lose his memories of the horrific occurrences
that took place in and under Derry Maine.

00:41:14.019 --> 00:41:18.430
At this point in the story, it is widely believed
that It, the creature that had caused so much

00:41:18.430 --> 00:41:21.180
pain and taken so many lives was dead.

00:41:21.180 --> 00:41:23.979
However, some might say that simply isn’t
true.

00:41:23.979 --> 00:41:28.109
Stephen King would go on to write many more
novels that either take place in, or reference

00:41:28.109 --> 00:41:31.920
the town of Derry, and some of them seem to
imply that the battle with the Losers Club

00:41:31.920 --> 00:41:35.560
in 1985 was not the end of Pennywise.

00:41:44.120 --> 00:41:48.560
A few years pass before the events of Stephen
King’s 1987 book The Tommyknockers, where

00:41:48.569 --> 00:41:51.479
an alien intelligence possesses the nearby
village of Haven, Maine.

00:41:51.479 --> 00:41:56.009
A fifteen year old boy named Tommy Jacklin
is sent with 13 year old Hester Brookline

00:41:56.009 --> 00:41:58.880
to retrieve as many car batteries as they
could manage.

00:41:58.880 --> 00:42:03.369
During the stop in Derry, Tommy notices a
clown with shiny silver dollars for eyes staring

00:42:03.369 --> 00:42:05.410
at him through an open sewer manhole.

00:42:05.410 --> 00:42:09.829
He brushes it off as an effect of the alien’s
mutations on his mind, but more evidence would

00:42:09.829 --> 00:42:13.329
come over a decade later in the year 2001.

00:42:13.329 --> 00:42:17.279
Dreamcatcher is another alien possession novel
by Stephen King in which a character named

00:42:17.279 --> 00:42:21.730
Mr. Gray -- which in itself could be a nod
to the human form of It, Robert Gray, comes

00:42:21.730 --> 00:42:25.539
across the former spot of the Derry Standpipe,
the water storage structure that was destroyed

00:42:25.539 --> 00:42:27.940
in the flood at the end of It in 1985.

00:42:27.940 --> 00:42:30.109
There’s now a memorial in its place.

00:42:30.109 --> 00:42:32.509
It reads, “TO THOSE LOST IN THE STORM.

00:42:32.509 --> 00:42:34.199
MAY 31, 1985.

00:42:34.199 --> 00:42:35.619
AND TO THE CHILDREN.

00:42:35.619 --> 00:42:36.970
ALL THE CHILDREN.

00:42:36.970 --> 00:42:41.710
LOVE FROM BILL, BEN, BEN, EDDIE, RICHIE, STAN,
MIKE.

00:42:41.710 --> 00:42:42.819
THE LOSERS CLUB.”

00:42:42.819 --> 00:42:47.079
But there is another message, which has been
spray painted in red jagged letters over the

00:42:47.079 --> 00:42:51.490
top of the memorial, which reads, “PENNYWISE
LIVES.”

00:42:51.490 --> 00:42:55.859
This is pretty solid proof that Pennywise
does indeed live on in Derry, because most

00:42:55.859 --> 00:42:59.980
of the town doesn’t know who Pennywise is,
and those who do don’t have the motive to

00:42:59.980 --> 00:43:02.630
deface this memorial, like Pennywise does.

00:43:02.630 --> 00:43:04.799
But how does Pennywise live?

00:43:04.799 --> 00:43:08.720
It was pretty clear that the Deadlights faded,
and It’s brandings disappeared from the

00:43:08.720 --> 00:43:10.819
door leading the spider’s lair.

00:43:10.819 --> 00:43:15.219
Some believe that the 27 year cycle simply
can’t be stopped -- that the Losers Club

00:43:15.219 --> 00:43:19.220
never had the ability to kill It to begin
with and that Pennywise simply went back to

00:43:19.220 --> 00:43:20.220
sleep.

00:43:20.220 --> 00:43:21.969
However, I have a different theory.

00:43:21.969 --> 00:43:26.680
At the end of the battle in 1985, Richie and
Bill finish off the spider while Ben stomps

00:43:26.680 --> 00:43:31.359
on all of the eggs, using only a pack of matches
to find and stomp out all of them.

00:43:31.359 --> 00:43:33.190
When they reconvene, Ben tells them.

00:43:33.190 --> 00:43:34.769
“I stamped out over a hundred.

00:43:34.769 --> 00:43:36.140
I think I got all of them.”

00:43:36.140 --> 00:43:37.769
“I pray to God you did.”

00:43:37.769 --> 00:43:38.769
Richie tells him.

00:43:38.769 --> 00:43:40.160
Then they flee the chamber.

00:43:40.160 --> 00:43:42.440
It seems pretty inconclusive to me.

00:43:42.440 --> 00:43:45.940
There’s even a thought at Ben has earlier,
as he’s stepping on them all.

00:43:45.940 --> 00:43:46.940
“How many?

00:43:46.940 --> 00:43:47.940
How many eggs?

00:43:47.940 --> 00:43:51.469
Didn’t I read that spiders can lay thousands…
or millions?”

00:43:51.469 --> 00:43:56.160
So I would theorize that at least one of these
eggs went unnoticed, and It was reborn into

00:43:56.160 --> 00:43:57.829
a new physical body.

00:43:57.829 --> 00:44:02.029
This new It would also have the shapeshifting
ability, and thus would also be able to take

00:44:02.029 --> 00:44:03.930
the exact same form as Pennywise.

00:44:03.930 --> 00:44:07.779
It also makes sense for the new It to use
this form again, because It seems to know

00:44:07.779 --> 00:44:11.499
all about things happening in Derry, and would
be able to pick up on the idea that the kids

00:44:11.499 --> 00:44:13.460
in town are scared of this clown.

00:44:13.460 --> 00:44:18.309
There’s one more possible piece of evidence
that Pennywise lives in Stephen Kings 2014

00:44:18.309 --> 00:44:20.059
book Mr Mercedes.

00:44:20.059 --> 00:44:23.930
This one doesn’t take place in Derry, but
rather, in Cleveland, Ohio where a serial

00:44:23.930 --> 00:44:26.359
killer wears a clown mask to conceal himself.

00:44:26.359 --> 00:44:30.319
One of the characters compares it to “the
TV movie about the clown in the sewers.”

00:44:30.319 --> 00:44:34.890
He’s talking about the TV mini-series adaptation
of It that came out in 1990.

00:44:34.890 --> 00:44:38.969
So apparently this adaptation also exists
in Stephen King’s universe, but you’d

00:44:38.969 --> 00:44:42.579
have to think that in order for that to be
possible, someone somewhere had to have seen

00:44:42.579 --> 00:44:46.670
the real Pennywise and been inspired by it,
so I see this as another piece of evidence

00:44:46.670 --> 00:44:51.479
that Pennywise is alive, probably as one of
the forms of the new It, after the events

00:44:51.479 --> 00:44:52.940
of the novel It.

00:44:52.940 --> 00:44:54.499
So what does that hold for the future?

00:44:54.499 --> 00:44:57.150
Could we one day see a sequel to It?

00:44:57.150 --> 00:45:00.640
During a Reddit AMA in 2013, Stephen King
addresses the question.

00:45:00.640 --> 00:45:03.349
“I don’t think I could bear to deal with
Pennywise again.

00:45:03.349 --> 00:45:04.999
Too scary, even for me.”

00:45:04.999 --> 00:45:08.739
So maybe we’ll continue to see Pennywise
lurking in the shadows in some of King’s

00:45:08.739 --> 00:45:12.720
future works, or maybe he’ll change his
mind after seeing how much people love the

00:45:12.720 --> 00:45:14.920
2017 and 2019 adaptations of It.

00:45:14.920 --> 00:45:16.920
Let me know what you think in the comments.

00:45:16.920 --> 00:45:20.289
Click the playlist on the left to see the
complete history of some of the other characters

00:45:20.289 --> 00:45:25.660
from It, and remember to subscribe to CZsWorld
for new horrors every week, ring the deathbell

00:45:25.660 --> 00:45:29.000
for notifications and I’ll see you in the
next one.

00:45:29.000 --> 00:45:31.499
Assuming, we both survive.

